{{ .Container }} --version
{{ .Container }} --help
```

A release is a wheel, `{{ snake .Container }}-<version>-py3-none-any.whl`, and its source,
`{{ snake .Container }}-<version>.tar.gz`. Install the wheel with
`uv tool install ./{{ snake .Container }}-<version>-py3-none-any.whl` (or `pipx install`),
which puts `{{ .Container }}` on your `PATH` in an environment of its own.
{{ end }}
## Develop

Open the repository in its devcontainer (`.devcontainer/`), which installs uv and runs
`uv sync` for you. Anywhere else, [install uv](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/getting-started/installation/) first.

```sh
uv sync                          # create .venv from pyproject.toml and uv.lock
{{- if eq .Type "worker" }}
uv run python -m app             # run it; Ctrl-C stops it
{{- else if eq .Type "job" }}
uv run python -m app             # run it once
{{- else }}
uv run {{ .Container }} -n Ada   # run it
{{- end }}
uv run pytest                    # unit tests
{{- if .Standard }}
make check                       # what CI runs: lint, formatting, types, tests and the build
{{- if eq .Type "cli" }}
make dist                        # the release wheel and sdist in dist/
{{- end }}
make help                        # every target
{{- else if eq .Type "cli" }}
uv build                         # the release wheel and sdist in dist/
{{- end }}
```

`uv.lock` pins every package; commit it with `pyproject.toml` whenever `uv add` changes them.

## Layout
{{ if eq .Type "worker" }}
- `app/worker.py` is the worker: `main`, the `[project.scripts]` entry point in
  `pyproject.toml`, sets up logging and the SIGTERM and SIGINT handlers and calls `run`,
  which does a round of `work`, then waits, until a stop is asked. Put the work of a
  round in `work`, or pass `run` your own; make a round safe to redo, since a crash
  repeats it. Tests call `run` with a fake `Stop`, and one sends a real SIGTERM.
- `app/backoff.py` holds the waits: `INTERVAL_SECONDS` between rounds, doubled per
  failure in a row up to `MAX_SECONDS`.
- `app/*.py` are the program's modules; `app/__main__.py` runs it as `python -m app`.
- `tests/` holds the pytest tests, one file per module.
{{- else if eq .Type "job" }}
- `app/job.py` is the job: `main`, the `[project.scripts]` entry point in
  `pyproject.toml`, sets up logging and calls `run`, which does `work` once and maps
  its outcome to the exit code. Put the job's work in `work`, or pass `run` your own;
  return when it is done and raise when it failed. Tests call `run` with fakes.
- `app/*.py` are the program's modules; `app/__main__.py` runs it as `python -m app`.
- `tests/` holds the pytest tests, one file per module.
{{- else }}
- `app/cli.py` is the command line: `main`, the `[project.scripts]` entry point in
  `pyproject.toml`, parses the flags with the standard library's `argparse`, writes
  results to stdout and errors to stderr, and returns the exit code (argparse exits 2
  for a wrong command line). Tests call it directly.
- `app/*.py` are the program's modules; `app/__main__.py` runs it as `python -m app`.
- `tests/` holds the pytest tests, one file per module.
- The name and version the program prints come from `pyproject.toml`.
{{- end }}
